boethius-1.logic.r1: argue/answered: U4: answered yes, which keeps boethius-1.logic.r1 and boethius-1.logic.r1.2, to: Does the text's argument take this for granted, whether or not it says so: "if (they would have been not less pleasing in themselves though never included among thy possessions and it is not so that they derive their preciousness from being counted in thy riches), then (if these things are beautiful in their own nature, then their beauty is nothing to thee)"? Answer yes if the author would accept it as part of the argument.
